  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moves along the quarter section of the circular path whose centre is at the origin. The radius of the circular path is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>. A force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> acts on the particle, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></math> denote the coordinates of the position of the particle. Calculate the work done by this force in taking the particle from point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> to point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>)</mo></math> along the circular path.<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image12-5456f7ad-bf7d-44a8-873a-f42e691e1f58.jpg\" />",
